source: genet, components/genet-livery/examples/capture_paint_corpus.rs
captured: yes — emitted by the real pipeline on 2026-08-10 (Livery CSS
  cascade, Taffy layout, Parley text shaping), not hand-built
describes: an article card at 320x240. Body background, a white card
  with a 2px solid border and 8px radius, an h1, two paragraphs, and a
  dashed top border on the last one.
covers: DrawText x4, DrawBorder x2, DrawRect x2, PushClip/PopClip.
  DrawText and DrawBorder are the point — no hand-written seed reaches
  either, and both are shapes only a real layout engine produces
  (glyph ids and positions from shaping, per-side border details from
  the box model).
payloads-elided: yes. FontResource carries raw TTF bytes inline and its
  own doc notes fonts run 100KB-20MB, so the faithful capture was
  2,037,474 bytes. Font and image payloads are replaced with a short
  stand-in; every command field is untouched. Verified rather than
  assumed: capturing with --keep-payloads and blessing produces a
  byte-identical .ops golden. Consequence: this fixture cannot be
  rasterized, only translated. Fine for the CPU tier; a constraint on
  any future GPU tier.
regenerate: cargo run -p genet-livery --example capture_paint_corpus --
  <this directory>
